---
import PlatformPicker from './PlatformPicker.astro';
/**
 * Overrides Starlight's `Search` — the header pair, and our own ⌘K modal in place of Pagefind's UI.
 *
 * WHY REPLACE THE DEFAULT: Starlight's search is a closed component. It can be restyled but it
 * cannot be given a RESTING STATE, and that is the whole of Stripe's modal — before you type it
 * already offers the page you were last reading and the questions people actually arrive with. An
 * empty box that waits is a worse answer than a box that guesses. The search itself is unchanged in
 * substance: same Pagefind index, queried through `lib/pagefind.ts`, the same one the hero uses.
 *
 * WHY THE BUTTON AND THE ASK BUTTON SIT TOGETHER: Oleh, 2026-08-18, from Stripe's docs — asking is
 * the same job as searching, one step further along, so the pair belongs where a reader's attention
 * already is instead of in a floating bubble.
 *
 * The dialog is moved to `<body>` at hydration. On the landing this whole row is hidden (the hero
 * carries its own field), and a modal nested inside a `display: none` ancestor cannot open — ⌘K
 * would be dead on the one page most likely to be a visitor's first.
 */
---

<div class="hs" data-pagefind-ignore>
  <button type="button" class="hs-search" data-search-open aria-label="Search the documentation">
    <span class="hs-search-icon" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8" /><path d="m21 21-4.35-4.35" /></svg>
    </span>
    <span class="hs-search-label">Search the documentation</span>
    <kbd class="hs-kbd">⌘K</kbd>
  </button>

  <button type="button" class="hs-ask" data-chat-open aria-haspopup="dialog" aria-expanded="false">
    <span class="hs-ask-icon" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
        <path d="M9.937 15.5A2 2 0 0 0 8.5 14.063l-6.135-1.582a.5.5 0 0 1 0-.962L8.5 9.936A2 2 0 0 0 9.937 8.5l1.582-6.135a.5.5 0 0 1 .963 0L14.063 8.5A2 2 0 0 0 15.5 9.937l6.135 1.581a.5.5 0 0 1 0 .964L15.5 14.063a2 2 0 0 0-1.437 1.437l-1.582 6.135a.5.5 0 0 1-.963 0z" />
      </svg>
    </span>
    <span class="hs-ask-label">Ask AI</span>
  </button>
</div>

<dialog class="sm" data-pagefind-ignore data-search-modal aria-label="Search the docs or ask a question">
  <div class="sm-field">
    <span class="sm-field-icon" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="8" /><path d="m21 21-4.35-4.35" /></svg>
    </span>
    <input
      type="text"
      class="sm-input"
      placeholder="Search the documentation"
      autocomplete="off"
      spellcheck="false"
      role="combobox"
      aria-expanded="true"
      aria-controls="sm-list"
      aria-autocomplete="list"
      data-search-input
    />
    <button type="button" class="sm-close" data-search-close aria-label="Close search" onclick="this.closest('dialog').close()">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="16" height="16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M18 6 6 18" /><path d="m6 6 12 12" /></svg>
    </button>
  </div>

  {/* THE SAME FILTER AS THE SIDEBAR, not one that resembles it (Oleh, 2026-08-20), and now
      literally the same control: `PlatformPicker` reads and writes the one stored preference, so a
      reader who narrowed to Notion on the welcome screen opens search already narrowed, and
      narrowing here updates the sidebar behind the dialog.

      IT IS VISIBLE rather than applied quietly. A filter carried in from another surface silently
      removes results, and a reader who does not know it is on reads the gap as "the documentation
      does not cover this". The control is the disclosure, which is why its collapsed form has to
      say what is on rather than the word "Platforms".

      NO `chipsUpTo` AND NO CHIP ROW, as of 2026-08-21. This surface used to render four inline
      chips because it had roughly 510px to spend and they fitted. They are gone with the prop: one
      question drawn two ways, depending on which surface the reader was standing on, cost more than
      the extra breathing room bought here. The disclosure is the control on all four surfaces.

      IT STAYS ON EVERY PAGE, INCLUDING THE ONE THAT NOW HAS ITS OWN (Oleh, 2026-08-21). The landing
      hero gained a visible `PlatformPicker` because a control that scopes the search must not be
      hidden inside it — and this one is the reason that diagnosis was right, so the temptation is to
      remove it here. It stays, for two reasons that are not preference. Every page but the landing
      has no hero at all, and ⌘K opens this dialog from all of them. And while this dialog is open it
      is in the top layer: the hero's control is behind the backdrop and cannot be reached or read,
      so suppressing this one would put the reader back in front of a search whose scope is stated
      nowhere — the exact defect. Two places, one stored value, never both reachable at once. */}
  <div class="sm-plat" data-search-platforms>
    <span class="sm-plat-label" id="sm-plat-label">Search in</span>
    <PlatformPicker label="Search in" />
  </div>

  <div class="sm-list" id="sm-list" role="listbox" aria-label="Results" data-search-list></div>
</dialog>

<script>
  import { wireSearchModal } from '../lib/search-modal';
  const d = document.querySelector('dialog[data-search-modal]');
  /* Out of the header before anything else: the landing hides the header row, and a dialog inside a
     `display: none` ancestor cannot be shown. */
  if (d && d.parentElement !== document.body) document.body.appendChild(d);
  wireSearchModal();
</script>

<style is:global>
  /* ── The platform filter row ── */
  .sm-plat {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--bo-base-300);
  }

  /* Starlight's prose rhythm margins every sibling after the first inside any flex box it reaches.
     This row is two children, and without the reset the control sat 16px below its own label. */
  .sm-plat > * {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .sm-plat-label {
    flex: none;
    font-size: var(--bo-t-12);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--bo-muted);
  }

  /* ── The header pair ── */
  .hs {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .hs-search,
  .hs-ask {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    height: 2.5rem;
    padding: 0 12px;
    border: 1px solid var(--bo-base-300);
    border-radius: var(--bo-r-8);
    background: var(--bo-base-100);
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
    font: inherit;
    font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  /* 18rem, not the 15rem this was: the label names its scope now ("Search the documentation", so a
     reader is not surprised when the board and the contact form never appear in it), and 15rem is
     narrower than that label plus the icon, the gaps and the ⌘K key. The button still sizes to its
     content — this is only the floor that stops the label being the part that gives way. */
  .hs-search {
    min-width: 18rem;
    color: var(--bo-muted);
    justify-content: flex-start;
  }

  /* The button is a fixed 2.5rem tall, so a label that wraps is a label with its second line cut
     off. Below 50rem the label is hidden outright and none of this applies. */
  .hs-search-label { flex: 1; text-align: start; white-space: nowrap; }

  .hs-kbd {
    padding: 1px 6px;
    border: 1px solid var(--bo-base-300);
    border-radius: var(--bo-r-4);
    background: var(--bo-base-200);
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
    color: var(--bo-muted);
  }

  .hs-search:hover,
  .hs-ask:hover { border-color: var(--bo-primary); }

  .hs-ask { font-weight: 500; flex: none; }
  .hs-ask-icon,
  .hs-search-icon { display: flex; }
  .hs-ask-icon { color: var(--bo-primary); }

  .hs-ask[aria-expanded='true'] {
    border-color: var(--bo-primary);
    background: var(--bo-soft-primary-bg);
    color: var(--bo-soft-primary-fg);
  }

  .hs-ask[aria-expanded='true'] .hs-ask-icon { color: inherit; }

  /* ── 50rem → 70rem: THE PAIR IS AN ICON PAIR UNTIL THE ROW HAS ROOM FOR THE WORDS ─────────────
     Oleh, 2026-08-26, from a tablet: the header was clipping. Measured on `/contact/` at 834, 900
     and 1024 — the whole band between Starlight's `md` (50rem, where it hands the header to the
     mobile treatment) and the width where the full row fits:

       header width      834 / 900 / 1024
       header content    1101   at all three
       .right-group      x=978 … 1101 — the account control ENTIRELY off-screen

     267px of header past the right edge, and no page overflow to give it away because the header
     clips. The expanded field is 348px of that; collapsed to its icon it is 84px, and the row's
     requirement drops from 1101 to 837.

     ── 70rem WAS THE FIRST ANSWER AND IT WAS TOO LOW ─────────────────────────────────────────
     1120 was derived from one page. It missed that the row's width depends on WHICH page you are
     on: the current pill carries `font-weight: 600`, so a long current label is ~10px wider than
     the same pill at rest. Measured at 1440 with the expanded field, `.header` content box 1392:

       /backups/how-backups-work/   current is `Docs`      nav 386 — fits exactly, no slack
       /contact/                    current is `Contact`   nav 396 — 10px over, and it CLIPPED

     Zero slack at 1440 on the widest laptop in the sweep, and a page-dependent overflow that only
     showed as a clipped account control. The row needs about 1460px to hold this field honestly.

     SO IT TAKES THE PRODUCT'S OWN NUMBER: 1599.98px, which is `collapsingSearch.ts`'s threshold in
     `apps/web` and one of the four declared widths in `specs/16-responsive.md` §1 — *"an empty
     toolbar search collapses to its icon"*. It was solved there for this exact question, it clears
     the measured 1460 with room for a longer label, and it mints nothing: this portal now shares a
     boundary with the product instead of inventing a fifth one.

     The precondition that rule carries is already satisfied here. `apps/web` checks that the search
     is EMPTY before collapsing it, because there a query in the field must never be hidden;
     `.hs-search` is a BUTTON that opens a dialog and can never hold a query, so there is nothing to
     check before folding it.

     `.hs-kbd` GOES WITH THEM, and not only for width: it names a shortcut the reader still has, but
     a bare `⌘K` floating beside an icon with no field is a label for a control that is no longer on
     screen. The dialog it opens states the shortcut itself. */
  @media (max-width: 1599.98px) {
    .hs-ask-label,
    .hs-search-label,
    .hs-kbd { display: none; }
    .hs-search { min-width: 0; padding: 0 10px; }
    .hs-ask { padding: 0 10px; }
  }

  /* ── The modal ──
     `is:global` because the dialog is moved to `<body>` at hydration and would lose a scoped
     stylesheet's attribute along with its place in the component tree. */
  /* `dvh` AND `dvh`, NOT `vh` (2026-08-25). On mobile Safari and Chrome `vh` is the LARGE viewport —
     the height the page would have if the address bar were retracted — and it does not change when
     the bar is showing. So `100vh - 96px` overstates the room by the bar's height, and `10vh` of top
     margin pushes the panel down by more than a tenth of what the reader can actually see: the
     search results run under the bottom bar on the one surface where the answer is the whole point.
     `dvh` is the live value and both readings want it. `vw` is left alone: the horizontal viewport
     has no equivalent problem, and under overlay scrollbars it equals `%` anyway. */
  dialog.sm {
    width: min(40rem, calc(100vw - 32px));
    max-height: min(32rem, calc(100dvh - 96px));
    margin: 10dvh auto auto;
    padding: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--bo-base-300);
    border-radius: var(--bo-r-12, 12px);
    background: var(--bo-base-100);
    color: var(--sl-color-text);
    box-shadow: 0 24px 64px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.4);
    overflow: hidden;
    display: none;
  }

  dialog.sm[open] { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }

  dialog.sm::backdrop {
    background: rgb(0 0 0 / 0.5);
    backdrop-filter: blur(2px);
  }

  .sm-field {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    flex: none;
    padding: 0 16px;
    height: 56px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--bo-base-300);
  }

  .sm-field-icon { display: flex; color: var(--bo-muted); }

  .sm-input {
    flex: 1;
    min-width: 0;
    border: 0;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--sl-color-text);
    font: inherit;
    font-size: var(--sl-text-base);
  }

  .sm-input::placeholder { color: var(--bo-muted); }
  .sm-input:focus { outline: none; }

  .sm-close {
    display: flex;
    flex: none;
    padding: 6px;
    border: 0;
    border-radius: var(--bo-r-6);
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--bo-muted);
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .sm-close:hover { background: var(--bo-base-200); color: var(--sl-color-white); }

  .sm-list {
    flex: 1;
    min-height: 0;
    overflow-y: auto;
    padding: 8px;
  }

  /* ── Rows (shared vocabulary — see `lib/rows.ts`) ── */
  .sm-list .sh-group,
  .sh-panel .sh-group {
    margin: 8px 0 4px;
    padding-inline: 12px;
    font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--bo-muted);
  }

  .sm-list .sh-group:first-child { margin-top: 0; }

  .sm-list .sh-row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 10px 12px;
    border-radius: var(--bo-r-6);
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .sm-list .sh-row[aria-selected='true'],
  .sm-list .sh-row:hover { background: var(--bo-base-200); }

  .sm-list .sh-row-body { min-width: 0; flex: 1; }

  .sm-list .sh-row-title {
    display: block;
    font-size: var(--sl-text-base);
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
  }

  .sm-list .sh-row-sub {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 2px;
    font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--bo-muted-strong);
    display: -webkit-box;
    -webkit-line-clamp: 2;
    -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  /* Pagefind wraps matched terms in <mark>; its default paint is a yellow highlighter. */
  .sm-list .sh-row-sub mark {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .sm-list .sh-row-icon {
    display: flex;
    flex: none;
    width: 32px;
    height: 32px;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    border-radius: var(--bo-r-6);
    background: var(--bo-base-200);
    color: var(--bo-muted);
  }

  /* The row that leaves the docs is the one that carries the brand. */
  .sm-list .sh-row-ask .sh-row-icon {
    background: var(--bo-soft-primary-bg);
    color: var(--bo-soft-primary-fg);
  }

  .sm-list .sh-row-hint {
    flex: none;
    font-size: var(--sl-text-xs);
    color: var(--bo-muted);
  }

  .sm-list .sh-note {
    padding: 12px;
    font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
    color: var(--bo-muted);
  }

  /* A button that reads as the link it functions as. It is a button and not an anchor because it
     changes state on this page rather than going anywhere, and a reader who is told the filter hid
     something needs the undo in the same sentence, not in the chip row above. */
  .sm-list .sh-note-act {
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    background: none;
    color: var(--bo-primary);
    font: inherit;
    text-decoration: underline;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .sm-list .sh-note-act:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--bo-primary);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }
</style>
